```python
@gene("s2", "where to walk: altar once carrying a worthwhile load (>=20 gems, late game, or winning tribute), else cleared-camp capture tiles, else living non-monolith gem camps, then gold camps, then any non-monolith group; leftover gems go to altar when nothing else to do", parents=["s2", "Z38a"])
def goals(mono: Tiles) -> Tiles:
    gm = gems()
    if gm > 0 and (gm >= 20 or round() > 1850 or team_gems() + gm >= 1000):
        acc = altar_goals()
        if size(acc) > 0:
            return acc
    acc = near(tile(-5, -5), 0)
    for g in range(num_groups()):
        if group_reward(g):
            acc = acc | group_tiles(g)
    if size(acc) > 0:
        return acc
    for g in range(num_groups()):
        if not group_respawning(g) and group_gems(g) > 0:
            gt = group_tiles(g)
            if size(gt & mono) == 0:
                acc = acc | gt
    if size(acc) > 0:
        return acc
    for g in range(num_groups()):
        if not group_respawning(g) and group_gold(g) > 0:
            gt = group_tiles(g)
            if size(gt & mono) == 0:
                acc = acc | gt
    if size(acc) > 0:
        return acc
    if gm > 0:
        acc = altar_goals()
        if size(acc) > 0:
            return acc
    for g in range(num_groups()):
        if not group_respawning(g):
            gt = group_tiles(g)
            if size(gt & mono) == 0:
                acc = acc | gt
    return acc
```

This mutation widens the threat zone that `progress` penalises. It keeps the cached `ECT` and adds a radius-2 halo around each healthy enemy champion, so the bot stops stepping right next to healthy enemies. The cost is one `enemies()` call per pass, since this zero-argument gene is recomputed every pass.

```python
@gene("Z109c", "threat zone: cached threat plus a radius-2 halo around healthy enemy champions, so progress avoids stepping next to them", parents=["Z109a"])
def enemy_champ_tiles() -> Tiles:
    out = ECT
    for u in enemies():
        if u.is_champion and u.health_frac > 0.5:
            out = out | near(u.pos, 2)
    return out
```
